st by South Africa’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/75289"} "Billie Legg"] " and then one by Wykoff. Williams took the lead off the start and was never headed, winning the gold over London, with Lammers third and Wykoff trailing in fourth. Two days later, Williams returned to win the " [:a {:href "/results/57619"} "200 metres"] ", the first non-American to complete the sprint double."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "667"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/66279"} "Percy Williams"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "11.0 (1 h12)"] [:td {} "10.6 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "10.6 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "10.8 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "469"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69257"} "Jack London"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "10.8 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "10.8 (2 h4)"] [:td {} "10.6 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "10.9 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "727"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/70374"} "Georg Lammers"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "10.8 (1 h9)"] [:td {} "10.8est (2 h6)"] [:td {} "10.7 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "10.9 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [: